# Public release tree.
#
# Deliberately NOT a copy of the private repo's .gitignore. That file carries
# `runs/*` with a `!runs/*/` re-include, which keeps per-run raw payloads out
# of the private history. Copying it here silently dropped the
# `runs/<period>.active` pointers from the first release commit, and without
# those pointers no stage and no check can resolve a run directory: a fresh
# clone failed claim-card-provenance with "no claim_cards.jsonl found" while
# the file sat right there on disk.
#
# The rule for this tree is simpler and safer. The release builder already
# decided what ships; everything it wrote to disk is meant to be committed.
# So nothing under runs/ is ignored here. Only genuinely local, regenerable,
# or secret things are.

# Credentials. The template ships, real values never do.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Python caches, created by running the test suites.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# LaTeX intermediates. Note manuscript.bbl IS a shipped deliverable.
*.aux
*.out
*.flc
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.nav
*.snm

# Rehydrated abstract payloads. tools/rehydrate_abstracts.py writes these
# from the publisher APIs under the user's own terms. They are not ours to
# redistribute, which is the whole reason only digests ship.
runs/*/private/01_abstracts.jsonl
runs/*/private/02_abstracts.jsonl
yearly/runs/*/private/01_abstracts.jsonl
yearly/runs/*/private/02_abstracts.jsonl

# Per-run build staging and generated gate-band config.
.staging/
staging/
.h1_config/

# Fault-injection sandboxes, one per mutation, regenerable.
sandbox/

# Local scratch and verification output.
scratch/
repro.txt
audit.txt

# OS noise.
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
